<section class="content-section">
  <h2>Feeding Your Cat Twice a Day</h2>

  <p>
    Establishing a consistent feeding routine is an important part
    of maintaining your cat's health and wellbeing. Feeding your cat
    twice a day, once in the morning and once in the evening, provides
    regular mealtimes and helps create a comfortable daily routine.
  </p>

  <p>
    Wet cat food is an excellent option because of its high moisture
    content, which helps support hydration alongside fresh drinking
    water. It also provides essential nutrients and comes in a variety
    of flavours and textures to suit different preferences.
  </p>

  <p>
    Divide your cat's recommended daily food allowance into two
    balanced portions. Serve one portion in the morning and the other
    in the evening, adjusting the quantity according to your cat's
    age, weight, activity level, health, and the feeding guidelines
    on the packaging.
  </p>

  <h3>Creating the Best Feeding Routine</h3>

  <ul>
    <li>Serve fresh wet food at consistent times each day.</li>
    <li>Use clean food bowls and wash them after meals.</li>
    <li>Remove uneaten wet food promptly.</li>
    <li>Always provide fresh, clean drinking water.</li>
    <li>Monitor your cat's appetite and weight to help maintain a healthy body condition.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    A regular morning and evening feeding schedule, combined with
    nutritious wet food and fresh water, can help support your cat's
    hydration, nutrition, and everyday wellbeing.
  </p>

  <p>
    <em>
      Kittens, senior cats, and cats with particular health needs may
      require different feeding schedules. Follow your veterinarian's
      recommendations for your cat's individual needs.
    </em>
  </p>
</section>

